# Monorepo conventions

## Layout

Keep code in the owning component directory. Do not invent parallel top-level trees.

- Contracts → `contracts/`
- Services → `ingestion/`, `cv-service/`, `activation-gateway/`, `control-plane/`, `ai-copilot/`, `cockpit/`
- Data → `lakehouse/`, `dbt/`
- Infra → `infra/terraform/{aws,azure}/`
- Observability → `observability/`
- Docs / ADRs → `docs/`

## README gate

Every **new top-level directory** must ship a `README.md` (purpose, how to run, ports, health check when applicable). Component READMEs stay accurate when ports, env vars, or entrypoints change.

## Commit messages

```text
phase-N: <summary>
fix(<component>): <summary>
```

Commit only when the user asks (unless a phase Definition of Done explicitly requires it).

## Phase discipline

- One phase per session unless the user explicitly says to continue.
- Each phase ends with passing tests and `PHASE_N_COMPLETION.md`.
- Do not pull Phase N+2 scope into Phase N.

## Host ports

**PRISM owns `9100–9199`.** Reserved map (extend in compose comments as services land):

| Port | Service |
|------|---------|
| 9100 | control-plane |
| 9101 | cockpit |
| 9102 | cv-service |
| 9103 | activation-gateway |
| 9104 | ai-copilot |
| 9105 | ingestion (status / metrics) |
| 9106–9198 | future / observability |
| 9199 | contract-stub / docs static |

## Secrets

Never commit secrets. Use `.env.example` + local `.env` / compose env injection.
